From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mediatek: describe MT6897 regulator resources

Describe the MT6897 regulator compatibles, resource limits and constants
used by the corresponding controllers and device trees.

Original-Commit: local development history
Original-Author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Original-Date: 2026-10-16T08:02:55+08:00
Original-Commit: local development history
Original-Author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Original-Date: 2026-10-16T14:05:36+08:00
Link: https://github.com/u0n0u/tb375fc-linux/commit/dfcba64529f973830a8bf435e823510f4e9491c6
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 .../regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml  | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..485155fc50
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/regulator/mediatek,mt6368-regulator.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: MediaTek MT6368 PMIC LDO regulators
+
+maintainers:
+  - AngeloGioacchino Del Regno <angelogioacchino.delregno@collabora.com>
+
+description:
+  LDOs of the MT6368 SPMI PMIC. The driver controls on/off and the
+  normal/low-power mode only; the constraints must state the voltage the
+  PMIC is set to (regulator-min-microvolt equal to regulator-max-microvolt).
+  VIBR (3.0 V) and VMC (1.8 V or 3.0 V) can only be set to those listed
+  values; VMCH is read back at 3.0 V.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: mediatek,mt6368-regulator
+
+patternProperties:
+  "^(vant18|vcn33-[12]|vibr|vmch|vmc)$":
+    type: object
+    $ref: regulator.yaml#
+    unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+
+additionalProperties: false
-- 
